# CLAUDE.md

Project rules for every Claude Code session in this repository, including the AI pipeline's agents.
Copy this file to `CLAUDE.md`, then replace the examples with your project's real rules. Keep it short: the
agents read it on every run.

## Project

- What this repository is, in two sentences.
- Main languages and frameworks.

## Commands

- Build and test: `./pipeline/scripts/run-checks.sh` (the same gate the pipeline uses).

## Architecture rules

- Example: controllers only map requests to commands; business logic lives in the application layer.
- Example: all database access goes through repositories.

## Conventions

- Example: follow the patterns of the surrounding code; match its naming and comment density.
- Example: every behaviour change comes with a test.

## Commit messages

[Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org): `type(scope): summary`, for example
`feat(api): add optional due dates to tasks`.

- Types: `feat` (new capability), `fix` (bug fix), `refactor` (no behaviour change), `perf`, `test` (tests only),
  `docs` (docs only), `ci` (CI workflows), `chore` (maintenance, tooling).
- Scope: the area changed, lowercase (for example `api`, `android`, `db`, `infra`).
- Summary: imperative, lowercase start, no trailing period, at most 72 characters.
- Breaking change: `!` after the scope (`feat(api)!: ...`) and a `BREAKING CHANGE: ...` footer.
- Footers: `Closes #123` or `Refs: #123`.

## Never

- Commit secrets, tokens or credentials.
- Change database migrations that have already run; add a new one.
- Edit `.github/`, `.claude/` or `pipeline/` from the pipeline.
